[=#firebirdprotocolversion]
= Protocol Version =

When a Firebird client connects, it offers a list of the protocol versions it can speak, and the server picks one.  Each version adds features, so client and server have to agree on which ones are in use.  The Firebird protocol module speaks versions 10 through 20 and defaults to 13.

The //maxprotocolversion// attribute of the listener tag sets the highest protocol version that the server will pick.  Values from 1 to 20 are valid.  Leaving it out, setting it to 0, or setting it to anything above 20 is the same as setting it to the default of 13.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-firebirdfeprotocolversion.conf@
}}}
}}}

Version 13 is the earliest version that supports [firebirdprotowirecrypt.html Wire Encryption].

Versions 14 through 20 enable untested or unimplemented features.  See [firebirdprotolimitations.html Limitations].

